153: ## 2. Logic Chain
154: 
155: 1. **Tokens & Theme Consistency (R1)**:
156:    - `web/src/styles/tokens.css:18` uses `cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1)`. In Tailwind CSS v4, `--ease-spring` under `@theme` defines utility `ease-spring`.
157:    - Replacing this with the 17-point CSS `linear()` curve (`linear(0, 0.006, 0.025 2.8%, 0.101 6.1%, 0.539 18.9%, 0.721 23.4%, 0.849 28%, 0.937 32.6%, 0.995 37.6%, 1.019 42.2%, 1.026 47.1%, 1.021 54%, 1.001 68.8%, 0.996 82.5%, 1)`) aligns all spring animations with physical specifications.
158:    - Defining Obsidian Horizon (`[data-theme='dark']`) and Tactile Alabaster (`[data-theme='light']`) variables with squircle radii (`--r-squircle-sm: 18px`, `--r-squircle-md: 20px`, `--r-squircle-lg: 24px`, `--r-squircle-xl: 26px`), specular rim catchlights (`inset 0 1px 0 0 ...`), proactivity tag tokens, and verb pill variables establishes a cohesive Hark Pro foundation.
159: 
160: 2. **Complete Mascot Removal (R2)**:
161:    - Search across `web/src` confirmed that `EyeTracker` is imported only in `HeaderBrand.tsx:2` and `LandingRoute.tsx:23`.
162:    - Deleting `.eyt*` styles from `tokens.css` (lines 256-336) and replacing `<EyeTracker ... />` with `<VigilSpark />` in `HeaderBrand.tsx` and `LandingRoute.tsx` completely eliminates the mascot artifact while preserving the minimalist `Vigil ✦` brand identity.
163: 
164: 3. **Urgency Rails & Verb Pills (R2)**:
165:    - `TaskCard` renders `NotificationCard`. By adding `urgency` and `proactivityTag` props to `NotificationCard`, `NotificationCard` can render a 3px leading border (`border-l-[3px]`) colored by `--urgency-*` and display the tag badge.
166:    - `TaskCard` action buttons can display active verbs (`action.verb || action.label`) using `.btn-primary` and `.btn-ghost` styling with squircle geometry.
167: 
168: 4. **Inline Approvals Without Navigation (R2)**:
169:    - `ChatRoute.tsx` previously redirected users to `/agent/approvals` on `chat.awaitingApproval`, which broke because `/agent/approvals` does not exist in `App.tsx`.
170:    - Creating `InlineApprovalCard.tsx` allows users to view the tool name, arguments, and trigger `decideApproval('approved' | 'rejected')` directly.
171:    - Mounting `InlineApprovalCard` inside `ThinkingCapsule` on `approval_required` and keeping `ThinkingCapsule` rendered during `chat.awaitingApproval` completes the conversational approval loop seamlessly.
172: 
173: 5. **Sandboxed Micro-Apps & Dashboard Pinning (R2)**:
174:    - In `ArtifactCard.tsx`, HTML/micro-app deliverables can be rendered inside `<iframe sandbox="allow-scripts" srcDoc={content} />`.
175:    - Adding a code/preview toggle and viewport switcher buttons (`375px`, `768px`, `100%`) provides the required responsive testing canvas.
176:    - Adding a "Pin to Dashboard" button stores pinned artifacts in a lightweight local store (`useWidgetsStore`), which `WidgetsRail.tsx` reads and renders on the Home surface.
177: 
178: 6. **Voice STT & Settings Connectors Studio (R4)**:
179:    - `InputPill.tsx` already has the microphone lifecycle and audio stream. Attaching `MediaRecorder` to `streamRef.current` allows recording audio chunks on press, generating an audio blob on stop, and sending it to `POST /api/v1/voice/transcribe`.
180:    - `ConnectorsSection` in `sections.tsx` already has access to `useMCPServers`, `useRegisterMCPServer`, and `useUnregisterMCPServer`. Adding the Vault management interface, 1-click Preset Gallery (`firecrawl`, `github`, `filesystem`, `postgres`, `linear`), and Custom Registration Studio delivers the full R4 client suite.
181: 
182: ---
183: 
184: ## 3. Caveats
185: 
186: - Backend schemas (`backend/src/modules/cards/data.py` and `backend/src/schemas/triage.py`) currently lack `proactivity_tag` and `verb`. The frontend types in `web/src/types/index.ts` should define them as optional (`proactivity_tag?: string | null`, `verb?: string | null`) so frontend works seamlessly in both mock simulation mode and live backend mode.
187: - In `InputPill.tsx`, `MediaRecorder` requires standard MIME types (`audio/webm` on Chrome/Firefox/Edge, fallback `audio/mp4` on Safari). Fallback mock handling is required so that voice input gracefully produces mock text when the Groq Whisper backend is offline or unconfigured.
188: 
189: ---
